 Qe("bip-0141.mediawiki", "consists of a 1-byte push opcode (one of <code>OP_0,OP_1,OP_2,...,OP_16</code>) followed by a direct data push between 2 and 40 bytes gets a new special meaning.", "The value of the first push is called the \"version byte\". The following byte vector pushed is called the \"witness program\".", "The scriptSig must be exactly empty or validation fails.", "The <code>scriptSig</code> must be exactly a push of the BIP16 <code>redeemScript</code> or validation fails.", "It is interpreted as a pay-to-witness-public-key-hash (P2WPKH) program.", "The witness must consist of exactly 2 items (≤ 520 bytes each). The first one a signature, and the second one a public key.", "The HASH160 of the public key must match the 20-byte witness program.", "The <code>witnessScript</code> (≤ 10,000 bytes) is popped off the initial witness stack. SHA256 of the <code>witnessScript</code> must match the 32-byte witness program.", "If the version byte is 0, but the witness program is neither 20 nor 32 bytes, the script must fail.", "If the version byte is 1 to 16, no further interpretation of the witness program or witness stack happens, and there is no size restriction for the witness stack. These versions are reserved for future extensions.", "the script must fail if the witness program has a <code>CastToBool</code> value of zero.", "Only compressed public keys are accepted in P2WPKH and P2WSH", "P2WSH allows maximum script size of 10,000 bytes, as the 520-byte push limit is bypassed.", "Comparing with the previous example, the scriptPubKey is 1 byte bigger and the scriptSig is 23 bytes bigger.", "its payment address is fully transparent and backward compatible for all Bitcoin reference client since version 0.6.0.", "programs with unknown versions are always considered as anyone-can-spend script, it is possible to introduce any new script system with a soft fork.", "will consider all witness programs as anyone-can-spend scripts", "Wallets should always be wary of anyone-can-spend scripts and treat them with suspicion.", "scriptPubKey: 0 <20-byte-key-hash>"),
 Qe("bip-0143.mediawiki", "The algorithm does not involve the amount of Bitcoin being spent by the input.", "the amount of data hashing is proportional to the size of the transaction", "While a 1 MB block would normally take 2 seconds to verify with an average computer in 2015, a 1MB transaction with 5569 sigops may take 25 seconds to verify.", "All sighash types commit to the amount being spent by the signed input;", "<code>FindAndDelete</code> of the signature is not applied to the <code>scriptCode</code>;", "<code>SINGLE</code> does not commit to the input index.", "the <code>scriptCode</code> is <code>0x1976a914{20-byte-pubkey-hash}88ac</code>.", "from O(n<sup>2</sup>) to O(n)", "1. nVersion of the transaction (4-byte little endian)", "10. sighash type of the signature (4-byte little endian)"),
